    ],
    [
     1,
     "Very late reply, but nevertheless:\r<br>\r<br>I tried to redo this using simulated data, and all went fine:\r<br>\r<br># population model (3 groups)\r<br>modelp &lt;- &#39;\r<br>    x10 ~ c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x1 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x2 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x8 + \r<br>c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x9\r<br>    x12 ~ c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x1 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x2 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x8 + \r<br>c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x9 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x14 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x10\r<br>    x11 ~ c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x1 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x2 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x8 + \r<br>c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x9 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x14 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x12\r<br>    x13 ~ c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x1 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x8 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x9 + \r<br>c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x2 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x12\r<br>    y   ~ c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x1 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x2 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x8 + \r<br>c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x9 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x10 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x12 + \r<br>c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x13 + c(0.7,0.8,0.9)*x14\r<br>&#39;\r<br>\r<br>Data &lt;- simulateData(modelp, sample.nobs = c(100,200,300))\r<br>\r<br>model &lt;- &#39;x10~x1+x2+x8+x9\r<br>x12~x1+x2+x8+x9+x14+x10\r<br>x11~x1+x2+x8+x9+x14+x12\r<br>x13~x1+x8+x9+x2+x12\r<br>y~x1+x2+x8+x9+x10+x12+x13+x14&#39;\r<br>\r<br>fit &lt;- sem(model, data = Data, group = &quot;group&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>bootstrapLavaan(fit, R=10, type = &quot;nonparametric&quot;,\r<br>                 FUN=function(x) c(coef(x), \r<br>standardizedSolution(x)$est.std),\r<br>                 verbose  = FALSE)\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>So either there is something funny with your data, or you did not show \r<br>us the whole script (the output was a single-group output, ignore \r<br>group=&quot;site&quot;).\r<br>\r<br>If you need us to investigate this further, we need a snippet of the \r<br>data, and the full script so we can reproduce the errors.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
